.TH ethercat "1" "2026-08-03" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
ethercat \- EtherCAT master command-line tool

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ethercat
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ethercat
is the command-line tool of the EtherCAT master built into LinuxCNC.
It inspects and configures the running bus: it lists slaves and their
configurations, reads and writes SDO entries, registers and SII/EEPROM
contents, transfers files via FoE, requests application-layer state
changes and rescans the bus.  This is the EtherLab
.B ethercat
tool adapted to talk to the master inside
.BR stmakd (1)
through its REST interface instead of a character device.
.PP
Commands can be abbreviated as long as they stay unambiguous.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B alias
Write alias addresses.
.TP
.B config
Show slave configurations.
.TP
.B crc
CRC error register diagnosis.
.TP
.B cstruct
Generate slave PDO information as C code.
.TP
.B data
Output binary domain process data.
.TP
.B debug
Set the master's debug level.
.TP
.B domains
Show configured domains.
.TP
.B download
Write an SDO entry.
.TP
.B eoe
Display Ethernet over EtherCAT statistics.
.TP
.BR foe_read ", " foe_write
Read a file from, or store a file on, a slave via FoE.
.TP
.B graph
Output the bus topology as a graph.
.TP
.B ip
Set EoE IP parameters.
.TP
.B master
Show master and Ethernet device information.
.TP
.B pdos
List Sync Manager PDO assignment.
.TP
.BR reg_read ", " reg_write
Output, or write data to, a slave's register contents.
.TP
.B rescan
Rescan the bus.
.TP
.B sdos
List SDO dictionaries.
.TP
.BR sii_read ", " sii_write
Output, or write, a slave's SII contents.
.TP
.B slaves
Display slaves on the bus.
.TP
.BR soe_read ", " soe_write
Read, or write, an SoE IDN of a slave.
.TP
.B states
Request application-layer states.
.TP
.B upload
Read an SDO entry.
.TP
.B version
Show version information.
.TP
.B xml
Generate slave information XML.

.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-master " \fILIST\fR"
Comma separated list of masters to select; ranges are allowed
(e.g. '1,3', '5\-7,9', '\-3').  Default: '\-' (all).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force a command.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Output less information.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Output more information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.  Use
.B ethercat
.I COMMAND
.B \-\-help
for command-specific help.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EC_INST
EtherCAT instance name (default:
.BR ethercat ).
.TP
.B STMAK_REST_URL
REST server URL (default:
.BR http://localhost:5080/ ).

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR stmakd (1)
.PP
The IgH EtherLab EtherCAT master documentation describes the master
architecture and the command set in full: https://etherlab.org/

.SH AUTHOR
Part of the LinuxCNC project, based on the IgH EtherLab EtherCAT master.
